# Normalise line endings on checkout, everywhere.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default) checks the
# repository out with CRLF, and every parser here that matches `\n` stops
# working: the docket frontmatter regex, the changelog's bullet and heading
# regexes, the track-scope diff. None of it shows up in CI, which runs on
# Linux with LF, so the checks pass exactly where they are tested and fail on
# the machine where rounds are actually started by hand.
#
# Found the hard way: the first scout run could not validate a single docket
# item, in a working copy where every committed blob was already LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish things that must not be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
